As far as I know, stealth only prevents sleeping monsters from waking
up on occasions.

Stealth is essentially inaudibility - the aural counterpart to
invisiblility. Thus I reckon that, unless the monster can see you,
stealth should confer the same evasion bonuses that invisibility
confers. And, if you have stealth and the monster can't see you, the
bonuses should stack.



